  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a small qualitative sample of twelve riders within a single local transit system, which may not capture the full diversity of transit environments and infrastructure.",
      "what": "Through semi-structured interviews and thematic analysis with 12 blind and low-vision transit riders, this study documents how vision-impaired individuals navigate and recover from unexpected transit disruptions. The research identifies five key themes regarding how these riders anticipate predictable issues, adapt to unpredictable events, rely on transit operators and fellow passengers, and utilize specific recovery techniques.",
      "why": "It documents the specific, lived strategies and technological shortcomings experienced by vision-impaired riders during transit disruptions, providing empirical evidence to guide the design of more inclusive, real-time navigation technologies."
    }
